00:50:52,950 --> 00:50:58,850
I ensure the messaging ladder is clear, the visual identity is aligned with the brand,

731
00:50:58,850 --> 00:51:02,750
and the media mix is optimized for the target audience.

732
00:51:02,750 --> 00:51:09,950
During execution, I monitor performance weekly, digital engagement, sales uplift, and feedback

733
00:51:09,950 --> 00:51:11,350
from the field.

734
00:51:11,350 --> 00:51:17,310
And finally, I evaluate the campaign's impact on the brand and document learnings for future

735
00:51:17,310 --> 00:51:18,310
planning.

736
00:51:18,310 --> 00:51:23,670
Can you share an example of a campaign that performed exceptionally well under your leadership?

737
00:51:23,670 --> 00:51:24,670
Yes.

738
00:51:24,670 --> 00:51:28,750
We were promoting a product in a highly competitive category.

739
00:51:28,750 --> 00:51:34,570
Instead of traditional ads, we built the campaign around real consumer stories.

740
00:51:34,570 --> 00:51:40,050
We worked with micro-influencers, created short-form content, and partnered with retailers

741
00:51:40,050 --> 00:51:41,390
for sampling.

742
00:51:41,390 --> 00:51:46,790
The authentic storytelling angle created strong emotional appeal.

743
00:51:46,790 --> 00:51:51,410
Engagement exceeded expectations, and the campaign delivered a significant uplift in

744
00:51:51,410 --> 00:51:53,590
trial and penetration.

745
00:51:53,590 --> 00:52:00,350
It reminded me that consumers respond strongly when communication feels relatable and human.

746
00:52:00,350 --> 00:52:01,350
Interesting.

747
00:52:01,350 --> 00:52:06,950
How do you manage innovation projects, especially when multiple stakeholders are involved?

748
00:52:06,950 --> 00:52:10,870
For innovation to succeed, alignment is critical.

749
00:52:10,870 --> 00:52:17,550
I start by building a solid case, consumer insight, market gap, feasibility, and business

750
00:52:17,550 --> 00:52:18,550
potential.

751
00:52:18,550 --> 00:52:25,710
Then, I work closely with R&D to test formulations, with procurement to evaluate cost structures,

752
00:52:25,710 --> 00:52:29,430
and with supply chain to confirm production capability.

753
00:52:29,430 --> 00:52:35,070
Throughout the project, I keep everyone updated with clear timelines and expectations.

754
00:52:35,070 --> 00:52:39,870
I've learned that innovation fails not because of lack of ideas, but because of

755
00:52:39,870 --> 00:52:41,750
poor coordination.

756
00:52:41,750 --> 00:52:46,670
I make sure everyone feels part of the process and understands the purpose behind

757
00:52:46,670 --> 00:52:47,670
the innovation.

758
00:52:47,670 --> 00:52:55,110
Let's shift to numbers. How comfortable are you with financial responsibilities like P&L or pricing decisions?

759
00:52:55,510 --> 00:53:01,470
Very comfortable. A brand manager is not just a creative role. It's also a commercial one.

760
00:53:01,470 --> 00:53:07,310
I work with finance to understand margins, cogs, trade spend, and ROI.

761
00:53:07,810 --> 00:53:11,770
When pricing changes are needed, I evaluate elasticity,

762
00:53:12,330 --> 00:53:14,990
Good morning. Thank you for joining us today.

763
00:53:14,990 --> 00:53:21,510
Let's begin with a quick introduction. Tell me about yourself and your branding experience.

764
00:53:21,510 --> 00:53:27,670
Good morning. Thank you for having me. I'm a marketing professional with experience in brand

765
00:53:27,670 --> 00:53:34,790
strategy, consumer insights, trade marketing, and new product development. I've worked in FMCG

766
00:53:34,790 --> 00:53:40,830
categories where I handled brand campaigns, market analysis, and full-year brand planning.

767
00:53:40,830 --> 00:53:47,830
I enjoy combining creative ideas with data-driven decisions to build strong, meaningful brands.

768
00:53:47,830 --> 00:53:52,830
Great to hear. Tell me how you usually assess the current performance of a brand.

769
00:53:52,830 --> 00:54:01,830
I analyze four key areas – market data, consumer behavior, competitor activity, and internal performance.

770
00:54:01,830 --> 00:54:09,830
I look at penetration, frequency, distribution gaps, region-wise sales and channel performance.

771
00:54:09,830 --> 00:54:16,230
Then, I evaluate consumer perception, brand equity scores, and digital sentiment.

772
00:54:16,230 --> 00:54:20,790
I also track competitor pricing, innovation, and promotions.

773
00:54:20,790 --> 00:54:26,350
This helps me identify whether the challenge is awareness, availability, affordability,

774
00:54:26,350 --> 00:54:30,230
or relevance, and then I shape strategies accordingly.

775
00:54:30,230 --> 00:54:35,630
Brand managers often balance long-term plans with short-term sales pressure.

776
00:54:35,630 --> 00:54:37,110
How do you manage that?

777
00:54:37,110 --> 00:54:39,870
I said clear KPIs for each.

778
00:54:39,870 --> 00:54:44,350
Long-term KPIs include brand equity, penetration,

779
00:54:44,350 --> 00:54:47,630
product roadmap, and strengthening positioning.

780
00:54:47,630 --> 00:54:51,270
Short-term KPIs include quarterly sales numbers,

781
00:54:51,270 --> 00:54:55,790
trade activation, availability, and tactical promotions.

782
00:54:55,790 --> 00:54:58,230
I make sure that even short-term promotions

783
00:54:58,230 --> 00:55:00,870
reflect the brand's strategic direction.

784
00:55:00,870 --> 00:55:04,370
Tactical moves should support the long-term narrative,

785
00:55:04,370 --> 00:55:05,830
not dilute it.

786
00:55:05,830 --> 00:55:10,610
Tell me about a situation where you helped a struggling brand recover.

787
00:55:10,610 --> 00:55:17,110
I once handled a variant that was losing share due to both taste issues and weak communication.

788
00:55:17,110 --> 00:55:21,670
I ran retail audits, consumer groups, and blind taste tests.

789
00:55:21,670 --> 00:55:27,650
The insight showed the product needed a better formulation and clearer value communication.

790
00:55:27,650 --> 00:55:33,510
We improved the recipe, upgraded the packaging, and launched a digital first campaign focusing

791
00:55:33,510 --> 00:55:35,710
on taste superiority.

792
00:55:35,710 --> 00:55:41,490
Within six months, repeat purchases improved, distribution picked up, and the brand regained

793
00:55:41,490 --> 00:55:42,930
lost share.

794
00:55:42,930 --> 00:55:46,850
How do you decide when it's time to refresh packaging?

795
00:55:46,850 --> 00:55:51,730
I look at consumer relevance, shelf standout, and functionality.

796
00:55:51,730 --> 00:55:57,210
If consumers say the pack looks outdated, if it blends into the shelf too easily, or

797
00:55:57,210 --> 00:56:00,850
if there are usability issues, it's time to refresh.

798
00:56:00,850 --> 00:56:06,570
But I ensure recognizability stays intact, so loyal customers don't get confused.

799
00:56:06,570 --> 00:56:10,570
A refresh should improve identity, not disrupt it.

800
00:56:10,570 --> 00:56:13,410
Cross-functional collaboration is important.

801
00:56:13,410 --> 00:56:14,810
How do you handle that?

802
00:56:14,810 --> 00:56:21,250
I work closely with R&D, supply chain, sales, finance, and procurement.

803
00:56:21,250 --> 00:56:27,490
I run regular check-ins, share clear briefs, and align everyone toward the brand objective.

804
00:56:27,490 --> 00:56:34,050
I believe transparency and clarity are essential when every team understands the why execution

805
00:56:34,050 --> 00:56:35,930
becomes much smoother.

806
00:56:35,930 --> 00:56:38,690
How do you typically brief an agency?

